.TH NONPAR 1
.SH NAME
nonpar \- Nonpareil HP Voyager calculator simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nonpar
.RI [ model ]
.RB [ \-display " display" ]
.RB [ \-data " directory" ]
.RB [ \-state " file" | \-nostate ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Nonpareil runs the original calculator ROM on a simulated Nut processor.
The native X11 interface supplies the original calculator face, mouse keys,
keyboard bindings, LCD segments and annunciators.
.PP
Supported models are HP-10C, HP-11C, HP-12C, HP-15C and HP-16C.
The default is HP-15C. For example:
.PP
.nf
nonpar
nonpar 12c
nonpar 16c -display 192.168.178.36:24
.fi
.SH CONTROLS
Press calculator keys with the left mouse button. Keyboard digits, arithmetic
operators, decimal point, Enter, Backspace and the numeric keypad also work.
The f and g keys select the calculator's shift functions. Escape operates ON.
F10 or the window manager's close command exits the simulator.
.PP
These are RPN calculators: to add 2 and 3, type 2, Enter, 3, +.
Keyboard shortcuts follow the upstream model's bindings. Function keys can
always be pressed on the calculator face.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-display " display"
Use the specified X display instead of DISPLAY.
.TP
.BI \-data " directory"
Read model directories below this directory.
.TP
.BI \-state " file"
Load continuous memory from this file, and save it on a normal exit.
.TP
.B \-nostate
Start with cleared memory and do not save state.
.TP
.B \-test
Run a ROM arithmetic check without opening an X window. Saved state is ignored;
an explicitly supplied state file receives the result of a successful check.
.TP
.B \-help
Show usage and keyboard controls.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /helios/local/share/nonpar
Calculator definitions, ROMs, original artwork and keyboard layouts.
.TP
.BI $HOME/np model .nst
Continuous memory, including registers, stored values and programs.
Each model has its own file, such as np15c.nst.
Two instances of one model should use separate state files when their
memories need to be kept separately; otherwise the last normal exit wins.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The GTK menus, other calculator families, plug-in modules, printer,
card-reader and sound interfaces are not included in this front end.
State files are readable text and are specific to this port; they are not
interchangeable with upstream Nonpareil's XML state files.
.SH AUTHORS
Nonpareil and its calculator simulators are by Eric Smith and contributors.
Artwork credits and licence notices accompany the installed data.
